                <pb facs="0810" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg702"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November 15, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received November 15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Terrell reports that the Turkish Government will relinquish the right of
                    imprisoning returning Turkish subjects naturalized in the <pb facs="0811"
                        n="703" xml:id="pg703"/> United States without the consent of the Sultan
                    since 1869 and will confine the assertion of its rights to expel undesirable
                    persons or classes of American citizens to such subjects.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
